==============================================================================
  #82 — THE FACTOR 10 IN g = 10*eps IS THE ROSTER SIZE N
==============================================================================

  N        = 10   (9 charged species + 1 vacuum seat)
  c        = (N-1)/N = 0.9
  fbar     = 2/pi = 0.636619772
  alpha_c  = 3 alpha = 0.021892058
  eps      = 0.012543225  (1.2543 %)
  g = 10*eps = 0.125432251

  G-A  the three factors reproduce eps = 27 alpha / (5 pi)
  ok    G-A1 eps = 27a/(5pi)   0.012543225115 vs 0.012543225115

  G-B  and 10*eps = 54 alpha / pi
  ok    G-B1 g = 54a/pi   0.125432251152 vs 0.125432251152

  G-C  the cancellation is exact: the 10 kills the census denominator
  ok    G-C1 10 * c = N - 1 = 9   10*c = 9.0
  ok    G-C2 so g = (N-1) * fbar * alpha_c   g is the UNNORMALISED total; eps is the per-seat average
  ok    G-C3 and g/eps = N exactly   g/eps = 10.000000000000

  G-D  ANTI-CONTROL: is N = 10 forced, or would any roster do?
  ok    G-D1 exactly one roster size reproduces g = 54a/pi   solutions: [10]
       -> so 'the 10 is N' is a constrained claim, not a relabelling:
          a different roster would give a different g, and does.
          N =  9  ->  g = 0.111495   (-11.1% vs recorded)
          N = 10  ->  g = 0.125432   (-0.0% vs recorded)
          N = 11  ->  g = 0.139369   (+11.1% vs recorded)

  G-E  the residual against the fit, stated not buried
  ok    G-E1 the closed form sits 4-5% above the minimiser's fitted g   closed form 0.12543 vs fitted 0.120  ->  +4.5%

==============================================================================
  ALL CONTROLS PASS
==============================================================================

  THE FACTOR 10 IS NOT A BARE INTEGER. It is N, the roster size the census already
  fixes -- nine charged species plus the vacuum's own seat. Substituting,

      eps = c * fbar * alpha_c        = (N-1)/N * fbar * alpha_c   -- PER-SEAT AVERAGE
      g   = 10 * eps = (N-1) * fbar * alpha_c                      -- UNNORMALISED TOTAL

  so g/eps = N exactly, and the 10 is the same 10 that sits in the denominator of
  c = 9/10. The two quantities are one sum counted two ways.

  IT IS FALSIFIABLE, WHICH IS WHY IT IS WORTH RECORDING (G-D). Exactly one roster
  size reproduces the recorded g = 54 alpha/pi; N = 9 and N = 11 both miss, so the
  identification is constrained rather than a relabelling.

  WHAT IS STILL OWED, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT QUESTION NOW. Not "why 10?" -- that is
  answered, the 10 is N. The open question is:

      WHY DOES THE S8 ROTATION-SHED COUPLING SEE THE TOTAL WHEN THE ELECTRON-MASS
      SHIFT SEES THE AVERAGE?

  That is a question about how each observable sums over the roster -- normalisation,
  not numerology -- and it is the same kind of question the corpus settles elsewhere.

  AND THE RESIDUAL STANDS. The closed form is 0.12543 against the minimiser's fitted
  0.120, i.e. +4.5%. Nothing here closes that gap, and the
  closed form remains FIREWALLED from the fit. This sharpens the debt; it does not
  discharge it.

